WEBVTT

00:13.687 --> 00:17.941
Well, young sir, I guess this is goodbye.

00:18.025 --> 00:20.694
Mm. But will you come back?

00:21.653 --> 00:22.654
Mm.

00:23.780 --> 00:26.450
Only if your family
still wants to hire me,

00:26.533 --> 00:28.785
once this child of mine
starts elementary school.

00:28.869 --> 00:31.580
I won't be as strong as I am now,
so I don't know.

00:31.663 --> 00:32.956
But I'll see you again.

00:33.665 --> 00:35.208
And when I do, young sir,

00:35.292 --> 00:37.878
you'll be so strong
you won't even need me.

00:40.255 --> 00:42.716
Be careful… of the dark.

00:56.688 --> 00:57.856
Dammit!

00:58.315 --> 00:59.441
That's not good.

01:05.739 --> 01:08.075
Well, it looks like it's stuck.

01:08.158 --> 01:11.578
I've already called for help, though,
so please don't worry, okay?

01:11.661 --> 01:15.040
But it's gonna take them four hours.

01:15.123 --> 01:16.416
Four hours?

01:40.315 --> 01:41.483
Nice one!

01:41.566 --> 01:42.567
You have great aim!

01:42.651 --> 01:44.194
Okay. Now what is it?

01:44.277 --> 01:45.320
What's my score?

01:45.403 --> 01:47.030
Come on, can't you just count

01:47.114 --> 01:49.199
the number of windows
that you broke yourself?

01:52.744 --> 01:53.578
Seriously?

01:53.662 --> 01:55.705
I was so close that time.
I can do this.

01:55.789 --> 01:58.250
Toshiro, you're trying way too hard.

01:58.333 --> 02:00.544
You shouldn't play strikeout
with the windows.

02:00.627 --> 02:02.504
Oh! Young sir.

02:02.587 --> 02:05.632
We didn't want to wake you,
so we went far from the bus.

02:05.715 --> 02:08.093
I guess you were still able
to hear us, though.

02:08.176 --> 02:09.970
You wanna play a round of ultimate bingo?

02:10.053 --> 02:11.054
Since you're awake now.

02:11.138 --> 02:12.639
Aren't you playing strikeout?

02:13.348 --> 02:17.018
Um, Kanaeno, um, did you just…

02:17.102 --> 02:19.146
Why did you call Akira "young sir"?

02:19.229 --> 02:21.106
Hmm…

02:22.190 --> 02:26.778
Well, ever since Akira here was little,
I've worked for the Yatsuka family.

02:26.862 --> 02:30.115
He used to be so scared
to go to the bathroom by himself,

02:30.198 --> 02:34.369
so I held his hand and took him there
when he had to go.

02:34.452 --> 02:35.704
Hey!

02:35.787 --> 02:37.164
Whoa! That was awesome!

02:37.247 --> 02:38.790
Another perfect strike.

02:49.009 --> 02:50.427
We gotta get out of here!

02:50.510 --> 02:51.970
What the hell's going on?

02:52.053 --> 02:53.972
Run! Faster, faster, faster!

03:06.026 --> 03:08.486
It said "Dr. Kudai and Ken Hikasa"?

03:08.570 --> 03:12.240
If you believe
in Toshiro's power, then yes.

03:12.324 --> 03:16.286
The Anti-Transfloration Movement
is who made Ivy, or, Mukuru Izumi.

03:17.037 --> 03:18.246
Those bastards.

03:18.330 --> 03:22.167
The public is angry
and the protests have been growing.

03:22.250 --> 03:24.127
The Transfloration Board is a mess.

03:24.711 --> 03:27.255
People will die if this continues.

03:27.339 --> 03:31.760
The higher-ups are now considering
downsizing Transflora Medical Number 4.

03:31.843 --> 03:34.012
If we don't uncover the truth soon

03:34.095 --> 03:36.723
and clear our names
of the false accusations made against us

03:36.806 --> 03:38.767
by the Movement, we'll lose.

03:43.396 --> 03:47.651
In order to win, we're gonna need to find
some solid evidence against them.

03:47.734 --> 03:50.028
We have to prove that
Ken Hikasa from the Movement

03:50.111 --> 03:51.738
and Dr. Kudai made Ivy.

03:51.821 --> 03:53.406
Ivy's Cultivation Report!

03:53.490 --> 03:55.116
The one written by the doctor himself!

03:55.200 --> 03:59.204
We won't be able to get our hands on that
unless we are able to find Dr. Kudai.

03:59.287 --> 04:01.164
He's been missing for more than 40 years.

04:01.248 --> 04:03.917
Okay. Well then, what should we do?

04:04.000 --> 04:08.171
What if we were to capture Ken Hikasa
and we interrogated him?

04:08.255 --> 04:10.382
I could be like a lie detector.

04:10.465 --> 04:12.300
That way we'd
find out the truth in no time.

04:12.384 --> 04:13.677
Hikasa has security.

04:13.760 --> 04:16.930
Well, actually,
it's more like a military unit.

04:17.013 --> 04:20.725
It's about five or six men,
and they're with him at all times.

04:20.809 --> 04:23.019
What if we asked the others
at Transflora Medical

04:23.103 --> 04:24.396
to help us out with this?

04:24.479 --> 04:25.355
Or the police?

04:25.438 --> 04:28.400
- We could ask your aunt, Akira.
- If we're gonna do that,

04:28.483 --> 04:31.778
then we'd need enough evidence
to put suspicion on the Movement.

04:31.861 --> 04:34.739
With what we have now,
nobody will do a thing.

04:35.949 --> 04:38.952
Then, the five of us
will have to handle this.

04:42.914 --> 04:46.293
All right, I'll go check out
the Archives, then.

04:46.376 --> 04:47.419
The Archives?

04:48.003 --> 04:50.046
Huh? What are the Archives?

04:51.840 --> 04:53.967
<i>It's basically a vault</i>
<i>full of secret documents</i>

04:54.050 --> 04:56.553
<i>that's inside of</i>
<i>the Transfloration Board building.</i>

04:56.636 --> 04:59.306
<i>The theoretical framework</i>
<i>behind Transfloration</i>

04:59.389 --> 05:01.057
<i>and it's early research are kept there.</i>

05:01.141 --> 05:03.268
<i>They want to prevent the public</i>
<i>from replicating it</i>

05:03.351 --> 05:05.562
<i>and abandoning the ethical standards.</i>

05:06.146 --> 05:08.315
The Transfloration system's black box.

05:08.398 --> 05:10.275
That's right,
and it might have information

05:10.358 --> 05:12.444
about Kudai's current whereabouts.

05:13.236 --> 05:15.989
I'll check out all the universities
and private companies.

05:16.072 --> 05:19.659
I want to try and find the lab where
the doctor created the Seed for Ivy.

05:19.743 --> 05:21.578
- Good.
- All right, well,

05:21.661 --> 05:24.080
I'll check if there's anything
at Transflora Medical.

05:24.164 --> 05:26.708
If we can find a clue
that leads us to the doctor,

05:26.791 --> 05:29.210
we'll have a chance of winning this thing.

05:32.047 --> 05:33.173
Let's do this.

05:34.299 --> 05:36.426
Down with Transfloration!

05:36.509 --> 05:38.178
Down with Transfloration!

05:38.261 --> 05:40.305
Down with Transfloration!

05:40.388 --> 05:42.098
- Down with Transfloration!
- Kudai.

05:42.182 --> 05:44.351
- Down with Transfloration!
- Kudai.

05:44.434 --> 05:45.852
Kudai!

05:48.104 --> 05:49.731
What? What was that?

05:51.024 --> 05:52.025
It looks like…

05:52.525 --> 05:53.985
we're not going home tonight.

05:58.907 --> 06:01.910
Yeah, I couldn't find anything here.

06:02.786 --> 06:04.412
And what about the Archives?

06:04.996 --> 06:07.540
<i>Ah, they wouldn't even talk to me.</i>

06:08.500 --> 06:11.211
<i>So, I guess I'll just have to try</i>
<i>a different approach.</i>

06:26.226 --> 06:29.646
The Transfloration system needs
to be abolished, once and for all!

06:29.729 --> 06:32.148
Transflora Medical should be shut down!

06:32.232 --> 06:34.651
Do you guys care
about anyone but yourselves?

06:40.740 --> 06:43.827
Do you think you have the right
to feel sad about this?

06:45.787 --> 06:49.124
<i>I will never forgive you.</i>

07:09.185 --> 07:11.855
HOSPITAL

07:28.830 --> 07:30.123
How much can I get for these?

07:30.748 --> 07:33.626
I did use some, but they're antibiotics
which are hard to get.

07:35.003 --> 07:37.672
Isn't that something
you'd want to keep for yourself?

07:38.381 --> 07:41.509
At the place where you work,
don't people collapse there every day?

07:42.802 --> 07:45.013
Yes, but I need money right now.

07:45.096 --> 07:47.265
I want to get my daughter and I
out of here.

07:52.312 --> 07:54.272
Do Spiriflora even need care?

07:54.355 --> 07:57.775
For Spiriflora that are
going to be placed in the city,

07:57.859 --> 08:00.153
the remaining skulls, spines,
and other undeveloped parts

08:00.236 --> 08:01.779
are removed to improve the appearance

08:01.863 --> 08:03.198
before they're transported.

08:03.281 --> 08:04.991
Wouldn't you be disgusted if those parts

08:05.074 --> 08:07.535
that didn't completely
undergo Transfloration

08:07.619 --> 08:09.537
were still stuck to the Spiriflora?

08:09.621 --> 08:11.581
If you become a Spiriflor, though,

08:11.664 --> 08:14.792
you can go back to the city
for a one-way shipping fee.

08:15.376 --> 08:18.046
We'd like to return
while we're still alive.

08:18.129 --> 08:20.882
Yes, well in that case,
you'll need a bribe

08:20.965 --> 08:24.677
for a high-ranking government official
to restore your credit history.

08:24.761 --> 08:25.803
How much is that?

08:26.846 --> 08:29.557
It's around three million yen per person.

08:35.146 --> 08:37.565
We only make 500 yen a day,

08:38.691 --> 08:40.068
so that's impossible.

08:42.445 --> 08:43.696
I don't get it.

08:53.289 --> 08:55.333
<i>I wake up at eight o'clock.</i>

08:55.416 --> 08:58.086
<i>Then from 9:00 to 12:00,</i>
<i>I scrape off the blood and flesh</i>

08:58.169 --> 09:00.129
<i>that's stuck to the beds and floors.</i>

09:01.714 --> 09:05.468
<i>When I'm done with that,</i>
<i>I eat soup that just tastes like salt.</i>

09:05.552 --> 09:08.221
<i>From 1:00 to 8:00,</i>
<i>I go around pulling the rotten limbs</i>

09:08.304 --> 09:10.306
<i>off of the vegetative patients.</i>

09:12.892 --> 09:15.812
<i>I only make 500 yen a day.</i>

09:15.895 --> 09:17.814
<i>If I save 200 yen a day,</i>

09:17.897 --> 09:20.525
<i>how long will it take to save</i>
<i>three million yen?</i>

09:44.507 --> 09:46.301
Meg?

09:46.843 --> 09:47.927
Meg!

09:48.344 --> 09:49.429
Meg!

09:50.805 --> 09:51.806
Meg!

09:56.311 --> 09:58.187
Meg!

10:00.231 --> 10:01.482
You're okay?

10:01.566 --> 10:03.151
I thought someone took you.

10:03.234 --> 10:05.862
Don't go anywhere without telling me.
It's dangerous.

10:07.989 --> 10:09.032
Uh…

10:10.908 --> 10:11.909
Meg.

10:14.662 --> 10:16.748
Did you get that money from…

10:18.207 --> 10:20.460
Why the hell would you do that?
That was so stupid!

10:20.543 --> 10:21.878
I had to!

10:22.211 --> 10:24.631
I want to get out of here, no matter what!

10:25.298 --> 10:26.466
How can you even…

10:26.549 --> 10:29.010
How can you say something
about the way I earn money?

10:29.636 --> 10:32.513
Don't you realize you're the one
who ruined my life, Dad?

10:32.597 --> 10:37.268
At this rate, it's gonna take
40 years to get out of this place.

10:37.352 --> 10:39.854
That means I'll be 55 when I can leave!

10:43.358 --> 10:46.486
I just want my life back.

10:53.534 --> 10:54.952
<i>Transfloration?</i>

10:55.495 --> 10:57.163
I'd be doing it for the subsidy,

10:57.246 --> 10:59.957
so that my daughter and I
can leave Paupertown.

11:00.917 --> 11:02.585
I've made up my mind.

11:03.753 --> 11:05.797
The success rate is low, you know.

11:06.923 --> 11:10.385
Plus, any personal use of the subsidy
isn't allowed here.

11:11.135 --> 11:12.929
What do you mean it isn't allowed here?

11:13.012 --> 11:13.888
Why not?

11:13.971 --> 11:15.723
I'm willing to undergo Transfloration.

11:15.807 --> 11:19.394
In Paupertown,
every person's Transfloration subsidy

11:19.477 --> 11:21.729
is split between a large number of people.

11:21.813 --> 11:24.440
If you were caught
by the town's authorities,

11:24.524 --> 11:26.776
they would confiscate all of your subsidy.

11:28.319 --> 11:32.240
They're nothing but a bunch of savages
who brandish iron pipes.

11:32.323 --> 11:34.242
You should have made this decision

11:34.951 --> 11:36.869
while you were still living
back in the city.

11:39.163 --> 11:42.250
Yeah, well even so, I'm going to do it.

11:44.210 --> 11:46.713
I'm gonna do what it takes
to get Meg's life back.

11:49.757 --> 11:51.509
I'm undergoing Transfloration.

11:52.176 --> 11:54.011
I'll come back here with the subsidy

11:54.762 --> 11:56.055
and we'll leave together.

12:08.776 --> 12:09.902
Thank you.

12:11.612 --> 12:13.865
Thank you so much, Dad.

12:15.992 --> 12:17.869
Thank you for doing this.

12:19.412 --> 12:20.538
Thank you.

12:23.458 --> 12:24.500
Hold on to this.

12:27.128 --> 12:28.421
Your watch?

12:28.504 --> 12:32.091
It was a gift from my grandmother,
and now I want you to have it.

12:32.967 --> 12:35.511
It doesn't show
all of the hours on here, though.

12:36.095 --> 12:38.431
It's how they used to make them
in the past.

12:39.056 --> 12:41.893
When the short hand
goes around once, it's morning.

12:41.976 --> 12:43.936
When it goes around again, it's night.

12:44.729 --> 12:45.938
All right.

12:46.522 --> 12:50.651
I was thinking, even if I'm gone,
you can sell it for a little bit of money.

12:59.702 --> 13:01.662
I'll be back soon.

13:01.746 --> 13:03.706
Take care of yourself until then.

13:06.542 --> 13:07.627
<i>I can go back.</i>

13:07.710 --> 13:09.212
<i>I can go back there.</i>

13:09.295 --> 13:12.215
To that warm and bright place.

13:12.298 --> 13:15.259
I can see my friends and my teacher again.

13:15.343 --> 13:16.469
I can see Saito.

13:16.552 --> 13:20.973
I can have scrambled eggs with ketchup
and consommé soup.

13:21.057 --> 13:22.975
Shopping malls.

13:23.059 --> 13:24.602
Clean water.

13:25.311 --> 13:26.354
A soft bed.

13:27.772 --> 13:29.732
Everything will be back to normal.

13:31.818 --> 13:33.277
Wait.

13:33.361 --> 13:34.654
Please.

13:35.822 --> 13:38.449
Don't cut off my right hand.

13:38.533 --> 13:42.370
I want to be… I want to… To draw.

13:42.453 --> 13:43.371
Don't take it.

13:46.165 --> 13:48.084
It's rotting, so I'm gonna cut it off.

13:57.134 --> 14:00.847
So, it's been two weeks already, right?

14:00.930 --> 14:04.100
Your father must have been caught.

14:05.518 --> 14:07.895
You're going to live here forever.

14:16.070 --> 14:17.446
Congratulations.

14:25.246 --> 14:29.667
How dare… How dare you laugh at me!

14:35.381 --> 14:37.091
Hey! Stop it!

14:37.174 --> 14:39.468
What the hell are you doing?

14:41.929 --> 14:43.055
You're fired!

14:48.477 --> 14:49.896
She's still alive.

14:51.063 --> 14:52.064
Take her.

14:55.443 --> 14:59.447
<i>Transflora Medical, Transflora Medical </i>

15:00.072 --> 15:02.241
<i>Even when your life is over,</i>

15:02.325 --> 15:04.535
<i>wouldn't you want to do something</i>
<i>to help someone else?</i>

15:04.619 --> 15:08.205
<i>Transflora Medical, Transflora Medical</i>

15:08.289 --> 15:09.415
Why?

15:10.499 --> 15:12.877
<i>Why did I say something so terrible?</i>

15:13.586 --> 15:15.129
<i>I said, "Thank you."</i>

15:17.673 --> 15:19.800
<i>Life never really ends.</i>

15:19.884 --> 15:21.177
<i>Life is a cycle.</i>

15:21.677 --> 15:24.430
<i>In exchange for a 10 million yen subsidy,</i>

15:24.513 --> 15:26.599
<i>why not offer yourself as a flower</i>

15:26.682 --> 15:30.269
<i>for the sake of the environment</i>
<i>and the future of humanity?</i>

15:30.353 --> 15:32.480
<i>Transflora Medical, Transflora Medical </i>

15:33.981 --> 15:36.108
<i>Even when your life is over,</i>

15:36.192 --> 15:38.903
<i>wouldn't you want to do something</i>
<i>to help someone else?</i>

15:44.075 --> 15:45.117
Okay.

15:46.702 --> 15:48.871
I'm done here. I couldn't find any leads.

15:49.789 --> 15:51.165
Yeah, same here.

15:51.248 --> 15:53.626
I wasn't able to find
any evidence, either.

15:53.709 --> 15:56.629
However, I found someone
who's close to the doctor,

15:56.712 --> 15:58.047
so we're on our way there.

15:58.589 --> 16:00.341
Yeah. Okay.

16:02.802 --> 16:03.803
Okay, listen.

16:04.345 --> 16:07.390
I was looking in the records
at the Transflora History Museum,

16:07.473 --> 16:09.892
and I found out
Kudai has a younger brother.

16:09.976 --> 16:11.227
That was a good find.

16:12.019 --> 16:14.105
Well, you gotta know where to look, okay?

16:14.188 --> 16:17.525
<i>In other news, a major policy</i>
<i>address by the Glory Days Party,</i>

16:17.608 --> 16:20.778
<i>the new political party formed</i>
<i>by the Anti-Transfloration Movement,</i>

16:20.861 --> 16:22.905
<i>is scheduled to take place in five days.</i>

16:22.989 --> 16:24.240
GLORY DAYS PARTY POLICY ADDRESS

16:24.323 --> 16:27.243
<i>Due to the incident involving a person</i>
<i>who underwent Transfloration,</i>

16:27.326 --> 16:30.121
<i>there've been many protests</i>
<i>at the Transfloration Board.</i>

16:30.746 --> 16:33.666
<i>Against this backdrop of social unrest,</i>

16:33.749 --> 16:36.752
<i>the upcoming speech</i>
<i>is attracting a great deal of attention.</i>

16:44.010 --> 16:45.928
The Glory Days Party?

16:46.012 --> 16:47.930
That kind of thing is pointless.

16:48.014 --> 16:50.433
It's never going to change anything.

16:51.100 --> 16:53.561
I'm… still going to protest, though.

16:54.562 --> 16:55.938
Seriously, Saito?

16:56.022 --> 16:57.606
My friend, Meg Okumura…

16:57.690 --> 16:58.983
Her life is…

16:59.066 --> 17:01.193
It's terrible now
because of Transfloration.

17:02.319 --> 17:04.947
Getting rid of it all together
would be for the best.

17:37.021 --> 17:38.147
STOP TRANSFLORATION!

17:38.230 --> 17:40.941
THE ROOT OF ALL THE TROUBLE
IS THE TRANSFLORATION BOARD!!

17:42.443 --> 17:44.945
MAKE THE TRANSFLORATION BOARD TRANSPARENT!

17:51.035 --> 17:52.953
MR. KUDAI

17:53.037 --> 17:54.663
You're Mitsuru Kudai, right?

17:55.331 --> 17:57.458
I'm Yomiko, from Transflora Medical.

17:58.501 --> 18:00.461
I'm Toshiro. I work there, too.

18:05.549 --> 18:07.426
I'll get straight to the point, then.

18:08.511 --> 18:10.763
Mitsuru, do you think you could help us?

18:10.846 --> 18:13.766
Do you have any idea where your brother
currently is at this moment?

18:13.849 --> 18:15.726
Dr. Otaro Kudai.

18:22.274 --> 18:23.651
<i>Hatred and fear.</i>

18:24.610 --> 18:26.028
Get out.

18:26.112 --> 18:29.156
I'm sorry, but can you at least
give us a yes or a no?

18:29.990 --> 18:30.866
Get out.

18:30.950 --> 18:31.951
We're not leaving.

18:32.368 --> 18:36.413
Mitsuru, listen, we wanted to throw
your brother in jail, that's why we're--

18:36.497 --> 18:37.873
Hey! Moron!

18:37.957 --> 18:39.542
Why would you say something like that?

18:40.167 --> 18:41.627
I see.

18:42.628 --> 18:45.548
If that's the case, you should've said so.

18:46.090 --> 18:48.300
I hate my brother. I always have.

18:48.384 --> 18:51.428
I would be happy to see him
thrown in jail before I die.

18:52.680 --> 18:55.307
But, I honestly don't know where he is.

18:56.225 --> 18:58.477
He lives off the grid
and doesn't have any way

18:58.561 --> 19:00.563
of communicating with the outside world.

19:02.439 --> 19:03.691
He's not lying.

19:05.860 --> 19:08.112
Why exactly do you
hate your brother so much?

19:08.863 --> 19:10.072
When we were children,

19:10.156 --> 19:13.617
my brother cut off two of my fingers
while I was sleeping.

19:13.701 --> 19:17.580
He did it because he wanted
to compare them to a book on anatomy.

19:17.663 --> 19:20.749
He doesn't understand other people's pain.

19:21.792 --> 19:23.836
Even after becoming a scientist,

19:23.919 --> 19:26.922
he was always consumed
with validating his own research.

19:27.006 --> 19:30.968
His obsession with that meant
he never gave a thought to anyone else.

19:31.051 --> 19:34.096
On the other hand,
after losing my fingers,

19:34.180 --> 19:36.974
I became even more sensitive
to other people's pain.

19:37.057 --> 19:39.018
<i>Anytime my finger joints ache,</i>

19:39.101 --> 19:41.729
<i>I feel like I can hear the cries</i>
<i>of the people suffering</i>

19:41.812 --> 19:43.689
<i>under the Transfloration system.</i>

19:43.772 --> 19:47.193
People who work at Transflora Medical,
like you two.

19:48.027 --> 19:50.321
You're really no better than my brother.

19:50.946 --> 19:52.823
You can't hear those cries.

19:55.117 --> 19:57.244
You're wrong. That's not true.

19:57.328 --> 20:01.457
Then tell me why you're still
working for a company like that?

20:01.540 --> 20:02.833
Uh…

20:04.960 --> 20:08.547
I've decided that I'm
going to vote for the Glory Days Party.

20:10.799 --> 20:12.968
I shouldn't be here.
I'm suspended right now.

20:13.052 --> 20:15.012
- Who cares?
- What?

20:15.095 --> 20:16.222
What's going on?

20:22.061 --> 20:24.230
This Spiriflor. Is it saying anything?

20:24.313 --> 20:25.481
Uh…

20:28.359 --> 20:29.652
Does it hate me?

20:31.362 --> 20:33.030
I don't hear anything.

20:33.906 --> 20:37.368
But it seems like it's able to tell
that you're… pretty tense.

20:38.369 --> 20:39.620
I see.

20:39.703 --> 20:40.829
Hmm.

20:46.043 --> 20:47.878
Did you hear something?

20:49.838 --> 20:51.632
I heard it say, "I won't forgive you."

21:08.565 --> 21:12.820
When I was in Paupertown,
I saw a lot of horrible things.

21:12.903 --> 21:15.781
It was a place consumed
by misery and madness.

21:16.156 --> 21:18.909
It was as if blood was
seeping out of the buildings.

21:20.202 --> 21:23.956
Akira, he said all that tragedy
was the embodiment

21:24.039 --> 21:26.000
of the Transfloration system.

21:26.083 --> 21:28.294
Some are sacrificed to save the rest.

21:30.170 --> 21:33.090
He said what we're doing
is bigger than ourselves, but…

21:33.173 --> 21:35.884
I don't feel like I'm part
of some grand cause.

21:35.968 --> 21:38.804
I'm just desperate
and I'm doing my best to hang on.

21:40.889 --> 21:41.724
SHIIKA

21:41.807 --> 21:43.809
<i>Even if I know someone else</i>
<i>is going to be miserable,</i>

21:44.601 --> 21:46.395
I can't seem to get off the train.

21:49.481 --> 21:52.109
Yomiko, do you feel like
this is a grand cause?

21:54.320 --> 21:56.363
I've always ridden the train
just pretending

21:56.447 --> 21:58.324
I'm oblivious
to what's really happening.

21:59.116 --> 22:01.118
I'm only working here to make a living.

22:02.953 --> 22:06.707
All that talk about
people giving up their lives

22:06.790 --> 22:09.084
for the environment and for oxygen.

22:09.752 --> 22:11.837
About passing life
on to the next generation…

22:13.047 --> 22:15.507
I only memorized that stuff
for the job interview.

22:20.637 --> 22:22.014
Should I get off the train?

22:27.895 --> 22:30.356
Don't you dare even think about it.

22:48.082 --> 22:52.711
<i>Toshiro… He knows exactly</i>
<i>what happens after you get off.</i>

22:54.421 --> 22:55.839
<i>You lose your seat.</i>

23:21.323 --> 23:24.993
<i>I want to make sure that</i>
<i>Toshiro is never miserable again.</i>

23:31.333 --> 23:33.419
<i>I swear that I'll protect him.</i>
